<title>USA: Moscom withdraws IPO for Votan subsidiary.</title>
<headline>Moscom withdraws IPO for Votan subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSFORD, N.Y. 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>MOSCOM Corp said Thursday that it has withdrawn its previously-filed initial public offering for its Votan subsidiary.</p>
<p>The telecommunications design and management company said the value being placed on its advanced speech technology unit was inadequate and didn't reflect the unit's full potential.</p>
<p>MOSCOM, which had planned to offer 40 percent of Votan to the public, said it will continue to operate Votan as a subsidiary.</p>
</text>
